    oe:aboutDisease oed:gastroesophageal_reflux_disease ;
    oe:answerText "Gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) is caused by the reflux of gastric contents into the esophagus due to a decline in esophageal clearance and anti-reflux barrier mechanisms. Mucosal injury is caused by a combination of gastric juice directly damaging the esophageal mucosa and the immune and inflammatory mechanism in which inflammatory cytokines released from the esophageal mucosal epithelium cause neutrophil migration, triggering inflammation."^^xsd:string ;
    oe:belongsToSpecialty "Gastroenterology" ;
    oe:cites oesrc:35226174,
        oesrc:35972481,
        oesrc:36927966,
        oesrc:39466255 ;
    oe:questionText "What is the recommended first-line pharmacological treatment for Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease?"^^xsd:string .

